(Protocol for Timing of Delivery in Pregnancy-Related Hypertension: A Randomised Comparison) Tj
T*
(of Maternal Experience Outcomes) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(This prospective trial aims to evaluate maternal birth experiences in women diagnosed with) Tj
T*
(hypertension during or prior to pregnancy. Participants will be allocated via) Tj
T*
(randomisation to either elective delivery at 38 to 39 weeks gestation or continuation with) Tj
T*
(routine antenatal monitoring until spontaneous labour onset or term. The primary) Tj
T*
(comparison will examine subjective measures of childbirth satisfaction across four) Tj
T*
(validated domains: personal agency during labour, quality of clinical support, sense of) Tj
T*
(safety, and level of involvement in decision-making. Secondary assessments will explore) Tj
T*
(free-text reflections from mothers and document any maternal or neonatal complications.) Tj
T*
(The trial will recruit from 42 maternity centres across the United Kingdom and aims to) Tj
T*
(enrol approximately 400 women. All participants will complete questionnaires postpartum,) Tj
T*
(with qualitative data analysed thematically. This design will provide evidence on whether) Tj
T*
(timing modification alters perceived birth experience in this high-risk obstetric) Tj
T*
(population.) Tj
